{"tool_name":"msnovelist","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"msnovelist","home":"https://github.com/meowcat/MSNovelist","license":"AGPL-3.0","summary":"De novo structure generation from mass spectra.","addition_date":"2022-09-05T21:19:03.847868Z","last_update_date":"2025-11-03T16:47:18.329938Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:msnovelist","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"zamboni@imsb.biol.ethz.ch","name":"Nicola Zamboni","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1271-1021","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Kai D\u00fchrkop","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9056-0540"},{"name":"Michael A. Stravs","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1426-8572"},{"name":"Sebastian B\u00f6cker","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9304-8091"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["recetox-specdatri"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Ab initio structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0476"},{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"Phasing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3454"},{"term":"Small molecule design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_4009"},{"term":"Spectrum calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3860"}]}],"name":"MSNovelist","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-022-01486-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022, The Author(s).Current methods for structure elucidation of small molecules rely on finding similarity with spectra of known compounds, but do not predict structures de novo for unknown compound classes. We present MSNovelist, which combines fingerprint prediction with an encoder\u2013decoder neural network to generate structures de novo solely from tandem mass spectrometry (MS2) spectra. In an evaluation with 3,863 MS2 spectra from the Global Natural Product Social Molecular Networking site, MSNovelist predicted 25% of structures correctly on first rank, retrieved 45% of structures overall and reproduced 61% of correct database annotations, without having ever seen the structure in the training phase. Similarly, for the CASMI 2016 challenge, MSNovelist correctly predicted 26% and retrieved 57% of structures, recovering 64% of correct database annotations. Finally, we illustrate the application of MSNovelist in a bryophyte MS2 dataset, in which de novo structure prediction substantially outscored the best database candidate for seven spectra. MSNovelist is ideally suited to complement library-based annotation in the case of poorly represented analyte classes and novel compounds.","authors":[{"name":"Bocker S."},{"name":"Duhrkop K."},{"name":"Stravs M.A."},{"name":"Zamboni N."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2022-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"MSNovelist: de novo structure generation from mass spectra"},"pmcid":"PMC9262714","pmid":"35637304"}],"topic":[{"term":"Lipids","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0153"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MSNovelist","home":"https://bio.tools/msnovelist","license":"AGPL-3.0","summary":"De novo structure generation from mass spectra.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:msnovelist/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online"